WEBVTT

00:02:32.230 --> 00:02:33.530
Yeah!

00:02:47.360 --> 00:02:47.540
Yeah!

00:02:48.400 --> 00:02:48.640
No!

00:02:55.560 --> 00:02:55.980
And...

00:02:59.440 --> 00:02:59.960
Hecatel!

00:03:00.000 --> 00:03:04.380
I'll be right here till the day I die.

00:03:07.390 --> 00:03:07.830
Spencer.

00:03:09.220 --> 00:03:09.620
Becker.

00:03:11.350 --> 00:03:11.670
Stack.

00:03:12.980 --> 00:03:13.160
Here.

00:03:13.630 --> 00:03:13.930
Lister.

00:03:15.780 --> 00:03:16.000
Here.

00:03:16.490 --> 00:03:16.830
Collins.

00:03:20.780 --> 00:03:21.060
Collins.

00:03:24.620 --> 00:03:24.920
Coy.

00:03:32.490 --> 00:03:33.810
I've been drinking every day now for a week.

00:03:34.960 --> 00:03:36.740
I used to like the rain when I was a kid.

00:03:37.370 --> 00:03:38.930
Even when it rained hard, like now.

00:03:39.590 --> 00:03:40.950
The last fight outdoors it rained.

00:03:41.570 --> 00:03:42.530
Slowed me up a lot.

00:03:42.840 --> 00:03:45.800
One of the most beautiful ladies I ever knew I met in the rain.

00:03:47.140 --> 00:03:49.080
High heels on wet pavement.

00:03:49.260 --> 00:03:51.030
Hey, here's your last look at Frank.

00:03:51.230 --> 00:03:56.120
They waste much time, do they?

00:04:00.030 --> 00:04:05.850
He muck lay, no more aches and no more pain.

00:04:06.580 --> 00:04:10.380
The good lord he treated Frankie very fine.

00:04:11.120 --> 00:04:15.470
He let him out before he finished his time.

00:04:16.050 --> 00:04:18.990
Well, gentlemen, that's one way of getting sprung.

00:04:19.170 --> 00:04:20.050
Maybe he's better off.

00:04:20.980 --> 00:04:25.900
I didn't think that even Captain Munzey would put a 62-year-old man to work in the brain pipe.

00:04:26.220 --> 00:04:29.060
Yeah, another dead guy compliments a Captain Munzey.

00:04:29.740 --> 00:04:29.980
Oh, what?

00:04:30.000 --> 00:04:31.500
He's on tap. There he is now.

00:04:32.280 --> 00:04:34.130
Joe. It's Joe with him.

00:05:19.880 --> 00:05:21.540
You and he were good friends, weren't you?

00:05:22.880 --> 00:05:25.160
He only had about eight months left to do, didn't he, Captain?

00:05:26.620 --> 00:05:29.480
Knowing McLean, out in eight months, back in nine.

00:05:30.800 --> 00:05:34.860
Right, Collins? Still carrying a grudge, eh?

00:05:35.140 --> 00:05:36.080
Lay off, Munzee.

00:05:37.630 --> 00:05:39.320
No, not Munzee.

00:05:39.660 --> 00:05:41.590
Sir, sir.

00:05:43.790 --> 00:05:45.750
You won't even meet me halfway, will you, Collins?

00:05:46.600 --> 00:05:48.740
Ten days in solitary, haven't taught you a thing.

00:05:49.070 --> 00:05:50.990
I better taught him not to carry a shiv anymore.

00:05:51.970 --> 00:05:54.030
Or do you still claim that knife was landed on you?

00:05:54.110 --> 00:05:56.110
Never mind that. The episode's closed.

00:05:58.480 --> 00:05:58.800
Collins!

00:06:00.350 --> 00:06:03.880
Why keep on fighting? After all, I've got a job to do.

00:06:04.380 --> 00:06:10.180
I'm... Very well. Have it your way.

00:06:23.780 --> 00:06:24.100
Joe.

00:06:25.720 --> 00:06:29.850
Dr. Joe, I meant to come down and visit you, but I...

00:06:30.250 --> 00:06:30.530
Yeah.

00:06:36.820 --> 00:06:40.300
Mr. Walters, there's a meeting this morning.

00:06:41.850 --> 00:06:43.030
Better get straightened out.

00:06:44.290 --> 00:06:45.170
The same to you.

00:06:57.970 --> 00:06:59.970
My old friend Joe was in...

00:07:00.000 --> 00:07:03.660
And it was worse than where they dig in coal.

00:07:03.900 --> 00:07:07.120
He comes out holding very high his head.

00:07:08.240 --> 00:07:12.360
And a man to blame soon be very dull.

00:07:23.440 --> 00:07:25.960
Joe, I'm glad you're back.

00:07:27.870 --> 00:07:28.430
Heard from the wife?

00:07:32.360 --> 00:07:33.400
Joe, you know Kid Coy.

00:07:34.270 --> 00:07:34.890
Seen him around.

00:07:36.330 --> 00:07:37.920
Moved him into Frankie McClain's place.

00:07:40.920 --> 00:07:41.740
Frankie was tops.

00:07:42.260 --> 00:07:43.140
Hard guy to follow.

00:07:44.190 --> 00:07:45.250
Whatever you say, Joe.

00:07:52.380 --> 00:07:53.740
Pidgeon, Joe. We made arrangements.

00:07:54.460 --> 00:07:55.220
Everything's okay.

00:07:56.620 --> 00:07:57.320
Everything's okay.

00:08:00.000 --> 00:08:03.730
What's okay? Nothing's okay.

00:08:05.520 --> 00:08:08.930
It never was and it never will be until we're out.

00:08:09.980 --> 00:08:10.380
Get that?

00:08:28.420 --> 00:08:29.860
Solitary. Even this will taste good.

00:08:31.790 --> 00:08:32.070
Thanks.

00:08:33.450 --> 00:08:35.290
No long talking to my mouthpiece yesterday.

00:08:35.510 --> 00:08:37.890
Your lawyer came all the way from the office to give you advice?

00:08:38.150 --> 00:08:40.350
Ah, ain't you heard? He's right here in the stir too.

00:08:46.410 --> 00:08:48.830
Roberts, I need a little help.

00:08:49.510 --> 00:08:50.490
Get away from me.

00:08:50.650 --> 00:08:51.710
But you're in with Gallagher.

00:08:52.670 --> 00:08:56.850
Please, Roberts, you know Gallagher can fix anything.

00:08:57.370 --> 00:08:59.410
There's some things that just can't be fixed.

00:09:00.250 --> 00:09:01.710
Roberts, if you could put in a word for me.

00:09:08.300 --> 00:09:09.240
Gallagher, I got to tell you.

00:09:09.790 --> 00:09:10.210
What does he want?

00:09:10.370 --> 00:09:10.670
Blow.

00:09:10.910 --> 00:09:11.850
Gallagher, you got to listen to me.

00:09:11.910 --> 00:09:12.630
I said blow.

00:09:12.790 --> 00:09:13.570
Kill me, they'll...

00:09:13.570 --> 00:09:13.930
Who is he?

00:09:14.530 --> 00:09:14.850
Wilson.

00:09:15.090 --> 00:09:17.490
He's here on a 529, also a stool pigeon.

00:09:18.040 --> 00:09:19.360
He planted a shiv on Collins.

00:09:19.380 --> 00:09:20.520
Munzey made me do it, honest.

00:09:21.660 --> 00:09:22.720
Fix anything, Gallagher.

00:09:22.860 --> 00:09:25.650
If you can call off Collins, I'd pay, I'd...

00:09:25.990 --> 00:09:26.590
You'll pay.

00:09:32.940 --> 00:09:58.120
Fritz, how's that cold coming along?

00:10:01.530 --> 00:10:01.850
Sir.

00:10:08.280 --> 00:10:08.920
Hello, Daniels.

00:10:09.150 --> 00:10:09.710
Morning, sir.

00:10:13.240 --> 00:10:16.560
Estrella, they tell me you're pressuring some of the inmates in your area.

00:10:17.080 --> 00:10:17.460
Am I?

00:10:18.640 --> 00:10:20.160
Captain Munsey, sir, I've got to talk to you.

00:10:20.630 --> 00:10:21.430
Please, sir, please.

00:10:28.460 --> 00:10:28.980
Morning, boys.

00:10:29.120 --> 00:10:29.640
Morning, sir.

00:10:30.830 --> 00:10:32.910
Oh, good morning, Gallagher.

00:10:33.880 --> 00:10:34.540
Morning, Captain.

00:10:35.340 --> 00:10:39.580
I understand you're responsible for settling that little feud over in cell block J.

00:10:40.780 --> 00:10:42.900
We appreciate your assistance, of course, but...

00:10:42.900 --> 00:10:44.460
The boys and I were only trying to help.

00:10:45.840 --> 00:10:47.100
You and your boys.

00:10:48.050 --> 00:10:51.770
There's a very old bylaw in this institution about gangs or cliques.

00:10:52.400 --> 00:10:53.220
We don't like them.

00:10:54.270 --> 00:10:55.010
We don't want them.

00:10:55.110 --> 00:10:56.430
Why don't you break them up, Captain?

00:10:58.490 --> 00:10:59.590
Gallagher, when...

00:11:00.090 --> 00:11:06.380
going to remember that you're not back home running a gang of hoodlums that may be the policeman eh you

00:11:06.880 --> 00:11:14.760
just serve your time and that way we'll both get paid off that's right captain the book says we

00:11:14.760 --> 00:11:29.600
always get what's coming to us all of us oh excuse me what's the matter with you wasn't

00:11:30.000 --> 00:11:30.480
Is that his fault?

00:11:38.870 --> 00:11:39.590
Sorry, Lister.

00:11:39.770 --> 00:11:59.690
The warden's breakfast ready and made with the ham and eggs and the marmalade.

00:12:08.870 --> 00:12:12.350
Sounds like a very important meeting you're going to do this morning, Doc.

00:12:19.900 --> 00:12:21.920
Is Captain Munzee going to be there?

00:12:24.220 --> 00:12:24.420
Mm-hmm.

00:12:30.000 --> 00:12:32.080
And he's the very best drink in the world.

00:12:32.380 --> 00:12:35.700
If you drink enough, your toes get curled.

00:12:37.760 --> 00:12:43.800
Calypso statistics show that if the level of alcohol in the blood exceeds one-half of one percent,

00:12:44.040 --> 00:12:50.720
the blood pressure is affected, a cerebral condition occurs, and then you're cockeyed.

00:12:54.970 --> 00:12:56.270
And maybe that's the way it should be.

00:13:09.468 --> 00:13:10.908
You don't like this, please, Doc.

00:13:11.868 --> 00:13:13.028
What for? You stay here.

00:13:14.044 --> 00:13:16.044
You haven't got much choice, Calypso.

00:13:17.116 --> 00:13:17.776
Neither have I.

00:13:23.164 --> 00:13:25.624
It's not as easy as all that, Mr. McCallum.

00:13:26.044 --> 00:13:26.684
This prison.

00:13:27.836 --> 00:13:29.956
This prison has almost twice as many men.

00:13:30.000 --> 00:13:31.300
as it was built to accommodate.

00:13:31.916 --> 00:13:34.256
There's not enough work to keep the inmates occupied.

00:13:34.416 --> 00:13:34.916
Why not?

00:13:36.364 --> 00:13:37.584
The world we live in.

00:13:38.252 --> 00:13:41.652
Yes, we can give them real work, teach them trades, produce things.

00:13:42.380 --> 00:13:44.940
But the civilian manufacturer says we're competing with him.

00:13:45.020 --> 00:13:47.500
Trade unions say we're putting their people out of work.

00:13:47.948 --> 00:13:48.788
Nobody wants to help.

00:13:49.004 --> 00:13:49.504
Not us.

00:13:50.444 --> 00:13:52.444
Manufacturers, unions.

00:13:52.684 --> 00:13:53.864
You might as well blame the weather.

00:13:54.764 --> 00:13:57.564
What you're really saying is you can't handle the situation.

00:14:01.244 --> 00:14:02.284
Excuse me, sir.

00:14:03.100 --> 00:14:05.400
I don't think you quite understood what the warden meant.

00:14:06.076 --> 00:14:08.236
It's not only a matter of controlling the men.

00:14:08.924 --> 00:14:10.024
He wants to help them.

00:14:10.268 --> 00:14:10.628
Muncy.

00:14:11.100 --> 00:14:13.060
What this prison needs is absolute discipline.

00:14:14.076 --> 00:14:14.676
Not charity.

00:14:16.220 --> 00:14:20.220
Your loyalty to the warden doesn't change the fact that he may be getting too old for his job.

00:14:20.412 --> 00:14:24.232
Age, Mr. McCollum, is a matter of arteries, not years.

00:14:24.572 --> 00:14:27.532
It's a pity, Walters, you're a better philosopher than you are a doctor.

00:14:27.964 --> 00:14:29.644
But I'm getting tired of you in both roles.

00:14:30.640 --> 00:14:33.780
I was sent here today for one reason, to tell you that if there's any more trouble,

00:14:33.920 --> 00:14:36.520
if this prison isn't brought under the strictest control...

00:14:36.520 --> 00:14:37.080
Mr. McCallum!

00:14:37.100 --> 00:14:40.500
There'll be an immediate change in practically all personnel.

00:14:40.820 --> 00:14:43.020
We don't want to be bothered anymore.

00:14:45.090 --> 00:14:45.750
Clear, warden?

00:14:45.750 --> 00:14:46.010
Yes.

00:14:50.330 --> 00:14:50.930
Clear to you, doctor?

00:14:51.890 --> 00:14:52.330
Oh, absolutely.

00:14:52.890 --> 00:14:54.790
You can't be bothered.

00:14:55.070 --> 00:14:58.340
Oh, that simplifies everything.

00:15:00.860 --> 00:15:02.020
The great public.

00:15:03.452 --> 00:15:04.452
and its servants.

00:15:05.404 --> 00:15:06.104
You put up.

00:15:06.268 --> 00:15:06.628
prisons.

00:15:07.036 --> 00:15:09.196
Thick walls, and then your job is over.

00:15:09.884 --> 00:15:11.884
finished.

00:15:12.732 --> 00:15:13.472
But is it over?

00:15:14.780 --> 00:15:17.280
You and your patent medicine remedies.

00:15:17.852 --> 00:15:19.012
Change the warden.

00:15:19.388 --> 00:15:20.328
New personnel.

00:15:21.180 --> 00:15:22.600
Absolute discipline.

00:15:23.196 --> 00:15:25.156
Do you know what this prison is, Mr. McCallum?

00:15:25.456 --> 00:15:26.936
One big human bomb.

00:15:27.256 --> 00:15:28.956
And you say, kick it and it'll be quiet.

00:15:29.308 --> 00:15:29.948
Smash it!

00:15:30.000 --> 00:15:30.840
that won't explode.

00:15:31.852 --> 00:15:32.252
Monty.

00:15:33.452 --> 00:15:35.152
What do you think of the doctor's viewpoint?

00:15:35.252 --> 00:15:39.052
I think, sir, that on occasion the doctor becomes unduly alarmed.

00:15:39.788 --> 00:15:40.108
One.

00:15:42.604 --> 00:15:43.604
I don't know.

00:15:46.028 --> 00:15:46.628
I do.

00:15:47.340 --> 00:15:49.260
Like so many dreamers and drunkards.

00:15:49.804 --> 00:15:51.264
The doctor's emotional words are empty.

00:15:52.140 --> 00:15:52.940
Watch your solution.

00:15:54.028 --> 00:15:57.708
What I know is that when people are sick, you don't cure them by making them sicker.

00:15:57.996 --> 00:15:59.996
By your methods, we send the man back to...

00:16:00.000 --> 00:16:02.580
a worse criminal than he was when they sent him to us.

00:16:02.780 --> 00:16:05.090
Platitudes, Doctor. I'm waiting for your solution.

00:16:05.980 --> 00:16:09.380
For men like you, Mr. McCallum, there will never be any solution.

00:16:09.500 --> 00:16:10.000
Wait a minute!

00:16:10.220 --> 00:16:12.140
Not why you want to destroy instead of build.

00:16:12.920 --> 00:16:16.420
What we need here is a little more patience and much more understanding.

00:16:16.750 --> 00:16:18.330
We've been patient too long.

00:16:19.060 --> 00:16:19.920
That's for understanding.

00:16:21.370 --> 00:16:23.830
I'm positive the purpose of my visit cannot be misunderstood.

00:16:25.270 --> 00:16:28.700
You'll remain here, Warden, only as long as there's no further trouble.

00:16:29.560 --> 00:16:29.880
Good day.

00:16:33.070 --> 00:16:56.810
Doctor, I'll see you to the gate sir. I've been warden here for such a long time. I don't know where to go.

00:17:04.060 --> 00:17:06.020
The place looks so nice now.

00:17:06.120 --> 00:17:06.760
Oh, that's swell.

00:17:06.980 --> 00:17:09.040
I got flowered drapes and a big chair.

00:17:09.180 --> 00:17:11.400
This boy doesn't know anything about it.

00:17:11.500 --> 00:17:12.320
Fine, fine.

00:17:12.560 --> 00:17:15.440
And if he did, it wouldn't matter.

00:17:15.500 --> 00:17:19.160
She loves to come to see you.

00:17:19.380 --> 00:17:20.620
It's good she's so young.

00:17:21.160 --> 00:17:23.100
She thinks it's such fun, like a holiday.

00:17:26.010 --> 00:17:27.380
Over there, your attorney.

00:17:32.460 --> 00:17:35.290
She won't go through with it. He's got to be.

00:17:35.290 --> 00:17:37.190
I've had three different doctors to see her.

00:17:37.640 --> 00:17:40.760
They've all tried to explain how important an operation is right away,

00:17:40.880 --> 00:17:43.640
but she keeps saying no, not unless you're there.

00:17:44.780 --> 00:17:47.750
Nothing matters to Ruth without you, Joe, not even her life.

00:17:49.450 --> 00:17:55.030
How long has she got? I don't know. Let me tell her you're here.

00:17:55.340 --> 00:17:59.140
No. She loves you, Joe. She'll understand. No.

00:18:00.730 --> 00:18:02.810
I guess you know what you're doing.

00:18:03.260 --> 00:18:05.520
Go back and talk. Try to make her go through with it.

00:18:05.880 --> 00:18:07.660
Keep trying, Joe.

00:18:15.240 --> 00:18:16.860
How much I can do, is there?

00:18:24.650 --> 00:18:25.670
I'm not trying to interfere.

00:18:26.820 --> 00:18:29.980
I'm just saying that if you send Roberts back to the drainpipe, I'll...

00:18:30.000 --> 00:18:42.480
I won't see. Have it your way. Joe.

00:18:47.680 --> 00:18:49.620
He'll find another job than he always has.

00:18:50.080 --> 00:18:51.780
Well, sit down. Be with you in a second.

00:18:52.710 --> 00:18:53.590
Glad you dropped in.

00:18:55.570 --> 00:18:58.290
Patient of mine. Old Pat Regan wants to see you.

00:18:59.400 --> 00:18:59.980
There's a pass.

00:19:00.030 --> 00:19:01.470
to the infirmary, right there on the table.

00:19:04.900 --> 00:19:05.260
Thanks.

00:19:11.060 --> 00:19:12.520
How quick will cancer kill somebody?

00:19:13.670 --> 00:19:15.550
Oh, that's the wrong way to put the question.

00:19:16.480 --> 00:19:18.700
These days, cancer doesn't have to mean death at all.

00:19:18.960 --> 00:19:19.240
Why?

00:19:20.280 --> 00:19:23.760
Well, how about if they have to operate?

00:19:24.260 --> 00:19:26.580
Even so, depends entirely on the case.

00:19:27.140 --> 00:19:29.400
The important thing, of course, is the time element.

00:19:30.890 --> 00:19:31.610
Somebody close?

00:19:32.290 --> 00:19:35.600
Yeah. By the way, what time is it?

00:19:36.310 --> 00:19:37.010
About 10.30.

00:19:38.540 --> 00:19:39.080
Are you sure?

00:19:39.700 --> 00:19:42.080
To be exact, it's 10.27.

00:19:43.800 --> 00:19:44.100
Why?

00:20:09.400 --> 00:20:10.320
Wilson, 10.30.

00:20:20.930 --> 00:20:21.870
Wilson, 10.30.

00:20:30.060 --> 00:20:31.300
Wilson, 10.30.

00:20:32.860 --> 00:20:40.890
Did I ever tell you about that last limousine of mine?

00:20:41.450 --> 00:20:41.890
Beautiful.

00:20:42.430 --> 00:20:43.110
That's roomy.

00:20:43.640 --> 00:20:46.940
Listen, that car was so long when I picked up the phone to talk to the chauffeur,

00:20:47.040 --> 00:20:48.320
I had to call long distance.

00:20:49.670 --> 00:20:51.770
Strangely enough, I had this same number on it.

00:20:52.720 --> 00:20:53.220
Keep moving.

00:20:56.170 --> 00:20:57.640
Wilson, 10.30.

00:21:00.030 --> 00:21:21.550
We'll go in.

00:21:22.060 --> 00:21:23.340
She does together, Frank Wilson.

00:21:36.170 --> 00:21:36.430
Hey!

00:23:25.050 --> 00:23:25.490
if it happened.

00:23:33.220 --> 00:23:36.940
Well, this is one rap they can't hang on you, Collins.

00:23:39.060 --> 00:23:42.920
I'm your witness. Important thing, witnesses.

00:23:44.820 --> 00:23:47.900
Lucky you asked me before exactly what time it was.

00:23:48.900 --> 00:23:51.550
Yeah, wasn't it? A fella named Wilson.

00:23:52.520 --> 00:23:58.430
Tough break. Accident? Positively. Witnesses.

00:24:21.540 --> 00:24:25.530
Remember that terrific third baseman who got paroled a couple of years ago?

00:24:25.830 --> 00:24:26.230
Dougherty?

00:24:26.350 --> 00:24:27.570
He'll be back for the book.

00:24:28.060 --> 00:24:29.160
He just knocked off his old lady.

00:24:30.030 --> 00:24:32.530
You don't say. Just shows you a guy don't think.

00:24:32.690 --> 00:24:35.830
If he done it last year, we might have beat the Patrolman's Benevolent Association.

00:24:48.910 --> 00:24:51.310
That's my advice about Wilson. I'd have said, don't do it.

00:24:52.230 --> 00:24:53.470
Maybe that's why nobody asked you.

00:24:53.820 --> 00:24:55.660
You only make things tougher for everybody else.

00:24:55.820 --> 00:24:57.200
I don't care about everybody else.

00:24:57.460 --> 00:24:59.900
That's cemetery talk. Why not? We're buried, ain't we?

00:25:00.700 --> 00:25:01.720
Only thing is, we ain't dead.

00:25:03.330 --> 00:25:03.930
It's on your mind.

00:25:08.480 --> 00:25:10.330
You and me, out.

00:25:12.580 --> 00:25:14.820
Tell me you've had the fever ever since the day you got here.

00:25:15.780 --> 00:25:17.300
