00:46:43.150 --> 00:46:44.610
The Department of Corrections.

00:46:45.660 --> 00:46:48.670
They've canceled all parole hearings indefinitely.

00:46:53.790 --> 00:46:54.270
What does this mean?

00:46:55.600 --> 00:46:56.180
Another year?

00:46:57.410 --> 00:46:57.550
Two?

00:46:58.500 --> 00:46:58.860
Five?

00:47:00.000 --> 00:47:04.710
Not necessarily. I'm sorry. It's not my fault.

00:47:04.890 --> 00:47:08.230
That is your fault! You've given in to Muncie all along the line!

00:47:09.380 --> 00:47:12.420
A couple of weeks ago, I stood here and you told me the gates were going to open for me.

00:47:13.000 --> 00:47:15.240
In just a few more days, I was going home.

00:47:16.640 --> 00:47:19.500
Home. I should have known better.

00:47:20.240 --> 00:47:22.000
Those gates only open three times.

00:47:22.560 --> 00:47:26.010
When you come in, when you've served your time, or when you're dead!

00:47:28.490 --> 00:47:28.930
Gallagher!

00:47:31.240 --> 00:47:32.580
Can I still count on your cooperation?

00:47:33.000 --> 00:47:41.700
Come here, fellas. Hi.

00:47:42.290 --> 00:47:43.790
I just got a pip on an assignment.

00:47:43.970 --> 00:47:46.870
I gotta write a story proving how good the chow is around here.

00:47:47.090 --> 00:47:47.870
You prove that.

00:47:48.650 --> 00:47:50.630
Time magazine will make you a man of the year.

00:47:52.770 --> 00:47:53.950
