Hiya, Tyrone.

00:48:53.390 --> 00:48:54.270
Hiya, Muggsy.

00:48:55.450 --> 00:48:57.190
You know, the way I got it figured out.

00:48:57.410 --> 00:48:59.600
Makes sense. What are you trying to say?

00:49:00.380 --> 00:49:03.520
Well, I got a favor to propose you.

00:49:04.250 --> 00:49:05.170
Don't ask me no favors.

00:49:06.190 --> 00:49:07.390
I can't be bribed, see?

00:49:10.680 --> 00:49:12.440
Besides, you ain't got enough dough to bribe me.

00:49:12.820 --> 00:49:28.970
I was once married to a dame like that, Bridge.

00:49:29.420 --> 00:49:29.980
What are you talking about?

00:49:31.320 --> 00:49:33.840
wonderful structure but up in the air most of the time

00:50:03.260 --> 00:50:03.600
Thank you.

00:50:31.660 --> 00:50:33.200
Backer, leave him alone. Get back to work.

00:50:33.520 --> 00:50:34.860
He's sick. He needs help.

00:50:35.080 --> 00:50:40.920
Back. I said get back.

00:50:42.760 --> 00:50:43.340
I'm all right, soldier.

00:51:21.720 --> 00:51:22.040
Take it.

00:51:30.250 --> 00:51:59.380
Hopping or buying?

00:52:00.000 --> 00:52:02.090
We're supposed to watch the men no matter where they are.

00:52:02.190 --> 00:52:04.050
In here, someone else watches after them.

00:52:04.470 --> 00:52:06.070
However, if you wish to stay...

00:52:06.070 --> 00:52:06.330
Thanks.

00:52:20.680 --> 00:52:21.620
We needed to open the gate.

00:52:23.300 --> 00:52:23.560
The gate's open.

00:52:23.840 --> 00:52:24.720
The bridge comes down.

00:52:25.510 --> 00:52:28.030
We all know there's no way out except over that bridge.

00:52:30.250 --> 00:52:36.800
First, we'll be here on the inside.

00:52:39.080 --> 00:52:40.260
We come out of the drainpipe.

00:52:40.630 --> 00:52:43.050
We'll be here on the outside.

00:52:44.100 --> 00:52:45.870
We hit the tower from both sides.

00:52:54.460 --> 00:52:58.090
One means they can't cover both sides.

00:53:00.190 --> 00:53:06.730
Once we take the vibe, all set.

00:53:11.660 --> 00:53:12.640
My men will know about you.

00:53:13.020 --> 00:53:14.340
I'm telling them only what they have to know.

00:53:17.650 --> 00:53:18.210
Gene, tomorrow.

00:53:18.440 --> 00:53:18.740
You're crazy.

00:53:18.940 --> 00:53:20.300
That's just what got a chance.

00:53:20.540 --> 00:53:21.240
This takes timing.

00:53:21.480 --> 00:53:21.640
Finding.

00:53:21.880 --> 00:53:23.810
No, the lock of the odds.

00:53:24.360 --> 00:53:24.720
Somebody calls.

00:53:26.110 --> 00:53:27.990
A third guy can't keep his mouth shut.

00:53:28.550 --> 00:53:29.650
No, for us it's now.

00:53:30.920 --> 00:53:59.870
As soon as we make it, the hour at 5th will need two minutes exactly.

00:54:11.140 --> 00:54:17.360
I know you got it all worked out, Joe, but don't we need a getaway guard?

00:54:21.310 --> 00:54:23.150
So these things, we'd be spotted right away.

00:54:23.350 --> 00:54:24.470
That's all I can tell you for now.

00:54:25.300 --> 00:54:27.460
We've been talking out for a long time.

00:54:28.400 --> 00:54:29.500
This is it, Joe.

00:54:30.350 --> 00:54:34.360
I don't want you to get sore, but, well, I've only got a short stretch left to do, and...

00:54:34.480 --> 00:54:36.360
There's no such thing as a short stretch.

00:54:36.500 --> 00:54:37.560
But you haven't told us much.

00:54:38.010 --> 00:54:39.910
We don't know how it'll work or what's supposed to happen.

00:54:40.410 --> 00:54:41.850
You're moving so fast that I...

00:54:43.250 --> 00:54:45.170
Say it. Pull out.

00:54:46.650 --> 00:54:47.510
I don't know any more than you.

00:54:47.910 --> 00:54:49.510
You declared yourself, and you can't quit now.

00:54:49.610 --> 00:54:49.890
Shatter.

00:54:50.140 --> 00:54:51.320
Don't misunderstand me, Joe.

00:54:52.910 --> 00:54:55.080
How many?

00:54:55.840 --> 00:54:56.000
Two.

00:54:57.010 --> 00:54:57.510
Play these.

00:54:58.490 --> 00:54:58.890
Three here.

00:55:02.560 --> 00:55:13.620
Spencer, in or out? Tees go at this.

00:55:14.400 --> 00:55:17.010
It's all or nothing, but you've got to make up your mind now.

00:55:17.830 --> 00:55:18.070
Now?

00:55:18.230 --> 00:55:24.950
You weigh no hard feelings.

00:55:27.960 --> 00:55:28.400
It's you, Joe.

00:55:30.640 --> 00:55:31.240
I'll play along.

00:55:31.420 --> 00:55:34.380
I thought different.

00:55:36.600 --> 00:55:37.240
Neither did I.

00:55:38.090 --> 00:55:54.430
Joe, what am I gonna do?

00:55:56.000 --> 00:55:57.380
Manage a couple of heavyweights, maybe.

00:55:58.340 --> 00:55:58.760
Who knows?

00:56:00.000 --> 00:56:01.900
I might even wind up owning a piece of a champ.

00:56:04.410 --> 00:56:06.800
All you guys will sit ringside, free.

00:56:08.260 --> 00:56:09.320
You're kidding yourself, Coy.

00:56:10.350 --> 00:56:12.890
Odds are, once we're on the outside, we'll never see each other again.

00:56:13.580 --> 00:56:14.560
Big city for me.

00:56:15.490 --> 00:56:18.230
When you've got millions of neighbors, nobody cares who lives next door.

00:56:19.490 --> 00:56:20.690
A fine or right dame.

00:56:28.870 --> 00:56:29.770
Henrietta be surprised.

00:56:31.760 --> 00:56:34.580
I think me and her will go away on a long trip.

00:56:35.240 --> 00:56:38.420
Sure. Most cons get married as soon as they get out.

00:56:38.840 --> 00:56:41.120
Married? Gee, I never thought of that.

00:56:44.120 --> 00:56:46.130
Hope you make it, Coy.

00:56:47.600 --> 00:56:49.020
You going back in the stock rack at Spencer?

00:56:49.750 --> 00:56:53.130
I think not. Printing costs are so high these days.

00:56:55.150 --> 00:56:59.140
Don't exactly know what I'll do. But yet, what about you, soldier?

00:56:59.710 --> 00:56:59.970
Me?

00:57:02.140 --> 00:57:08.940
I got a long way to go. Ever since the war, I've been trying to get back to a little town in Italy.

00:57:12.000 --> 00:57:16.520
But you know how the breaks go. With me, one rap led to another.

00:57:18.580 --> 00:57:23.680
Anyway, I was never able to make it. Maybe this time.

00:57:47.920 --> 00:57:50.120
Robert, you must go away. The military police, they were here.

00:57:53.550 --> 00:57:55.820
How long ago? What did they say?

00:57:55.980 --> 00:57:57.420
I talked to them, it was nothing.

00:57:57.800 --> 00:57:59.560
A more important thing.

00:58:00.000 --> 00:58:01.180
He brought no food, he is leaving.

00:58:01.360 --> 00:58:01.700
So?

00:58:02.200 --> 00:58:03.380
Food's out there in the truck.

00:58:03.790 --> 00:58:04.130
Thank you.

00:58:04.310 --> 00:58:04.550
No!

00:58:05.140 --> 00:58:06.000
You will take nothing.

00:58:06.220 --> 00:58:07.520
You will stand in line with the others.

00:58:07.760 --> 00:58:08.740
When there is food, you will eat.

00:58:08.900 --> 00:58:09.960
And when there is no food?

00:58:10.120 --> 00:58:11.380
Then you will starve with the others.

00:58:12.750 --> 00:58:14.890
We're not all so fortunate as you, my daughter.

00:58:15.090 --> 00:58:17.490
We have no great love to quiet our appetites.

00:58:17.940 --> 00:58:19.000
Robert does not object.

00:58:19.140 --> 00:58:19.600
Why do you?

00:58:20.190 --> 00:58:21.890
He does not know you so well as I.

00:58:24.220 --> 00:58:27.800
Is it so great a crime to accept food from those who deprived you of it?

00:58:28.630 --> 00:58:29.970
Nothing personal, of course, but...

00:58:30.000 --> 00:58:34.400
But since you do not spare the bombs, we do not expect you to spare the food.

00:58:35.250 --> 00:58:36.510
You Americans are such a generous...

00:58:36.510 --> 00:58:38.890
Don't mind the speeches. The food's out there. Go get it.

00:58:39.010 --> 00:58:41.880
No. He hates you, Robert. He hates your uniform.

00:58:42.100 --> 00:58:44.260
He fought you in Sicily. He still fights you.

00:58:44.550 --> 00:58:46.830
My position does not permit me to hate anyone.

00:59:00.830 --> 00:59:02.350
I'm foolish, so I cry.

00:59:03.100 --> 00:59:05.380
It's nothing. In a war, people cry easy.

00:59:07.720 --> 00:59:09.340
Promise me you won't come here again.

00:59:10.680 --> 00:59:15.800
If the police should find you, bringing us food this way is against the law.

00:59:17.970 --> 00:59:21.390
The law is second. My wife comes first.

00:59:39.080 --> 00:59:46.760
they're back say nothing about it you understand robert is a stranger we never saw him before

00:59:46.760 --> 00:59:50.780
he stopped here for water water for the truck and if they discovered i was lying what then

00:59:50.780 --> 00:59:55.940
why should i raise my leg for you because i stuck mine out for you for me no signora you

00:59:55.940 --> 00:59:59.880
came to see her i will not lie for you you and your police can

01:00:00.000 --> 01:00:11.870
destroy each other. Gina, keep him here. I'll get the water. If they believe me, I've got a chance.

01:00:30.090 --> 01:00:37.880
Hey, soldier! Hey, soldier! Snap out of it!

01:00:38.950 --> 01:00:40.410
You're missing a swell yarn!

01:00:42.000 --> 01:00:42.840
Go ahead, Spencer.

01:00:43.380 --> 01:00:48.380
Well, gentlemen, as I was saying, there I was, besieged on all sides,

01:00:48.840 --> 01:00:52.000
the citizens to the front, the howling investors behind me,

01:00:52.350 --> 01:00:56.820
the sheriff's men closing in, but I remained undaunted,

01:00:57.740 --> 01:00:59.960
smiling, secure in my right.

01:01:00.000 --> 01:01:01.230
What happened?

01:01:02.860 --> 01:01:03.420
Here I am.

01:01:04.310 --> 01:01:05.970
Okay, break it up. Let's try to get some sleep.

01:01:06.180 --> 01:01:06.480
Why?

01:01:06.950 --> 01:01:08.450
I like to hear Spitzer talk.

01:01:08.780 --> 01:01:09.640
Talk too much already.

01:01:10.480 --> 01:01:11.760
There are ears all over this drum.

01:01:12.100 --> 01:01:13.220
They all belong to one guy.

01:01:16.420 --> 01:01:17.520
What's the answer to it?

01:01:17.990 --> 01:01:20.270
Are we going to have to keep every prisoner in virtual solitary?

01:01:21.330 --> 01:01:23.290
Other prisons must have these same problems,

01:01:23.410 --> 01:01:25.330
but they clear them up, keep things running smoothly.

01:01:25.610 --> 01:01:27.730
We've been through difficult times before, Ward.

01:01:27.850 --> 01:01:28.830
Oh, never like this.

01:01:30.000 --> 01:01:33.770
McCallum is coming. Why? I can't even let me alone.

01:01:35.870 --> 01:01:36.770
Everything's gone wrong.

01:01:38.940 --> 01:01:45.050
I don't know who's to blame, but I do know that every prisoner hates us.

01:01:45.960 --> 01:01:49.040
Not us. Me. It's me they hate.

01:01:49.630 --> 01:01:50.650
I wonder why.

01:01:50.930 --> 01:01:59.000
You put on a guard's uniform and see how much they love you.

01:02:01.980 --> 01:02:04.920
You talk to the prisoners over a loudspeaker, I talk to them with a club.

01:02:05.250 --> 01:02:08.070
You only make the rules. I have to enforce them.

01:02:08.320 --> 01:02:09.600
Maybe it's the way you enforce them.

01:02:11.340 --> 01:02:12.020
Maybe it is.

01:02:13.350 --> 01:02:16.720
Oh, I'm not criticizing Munzi, it's just that...

01:02:16.720 --> 01:02:19.070
But you are, and perhaps you're right.

01:02:20.780 --> 01:02:23.720
All I know is that I've tried to do my job as I saw it,

01:02:24.720 --> 01:02:26.260
but if I'm the cause of this trouble,

01:02:26.790 --> 01:02:29.970
if I'm wrong and those convicts are right, then...

01:02:30.000 --> 01:02:31.440
you can have my resignation immediately.

01:02:31.980 --> 01:02:34.400
No, Munzee, that's just what the inmates would like.

01:02:34.500 --> 01:02:35.540
No, no, that's not the answer.

01:02:36.390 --> 01:02:38.610
As you said, we've been through some difficult times together here.

01:02:38.730 --> 01:02:41.230
Well, we're still here and we're still together.

01:02:42.960 --> 01:02:44.810
Let's leave it that way.

01:02:47.700 --> 01:02:52.230
The situation seems to call for a drink, warden.

01:02:53.250 --> 01:02:56.680
Thanks, I'm going to turn in.

01:02:56.820 --> 01:02:56.980
Good night.

01:02:58.060 --> 01:02:59.960
Don't be discouraged, warden.

01:03:00.640 --> 01:03:02.660
It's a rule in all the best stories.

01:03:03.520 --> 01:03:06.280
Everybody always lives happily ever after.

01:03:08.460 --> 01:03:08.720
Good night.

01:03:13.690 --> 01:03:16.390
You don't believe I meant what I said about resigning, do you, Doctor?

01:03:17.210 --> 01:03:19.800
In a million words, no.

01:03:21.930 --> 01:03:22.470
You're wrong.

01:03:23.900 --> 01:03:25.300
I really want to help the warden.

01:03:26.480 --> 01:03:28.200
Just that he's confused.

01:03:30.190 --> 01:03:33.100
He doesn't know that kindness is actually weakness.

01:03:34.400 --> 01:03:38.100
And weakness is an infection that makes a man a follower instead of a leader.

01:03:38.710 --> 01:03:41.410
Seems to me a very great leader once said,

01:03:41.450 --> 01:03:43.130
the meek shall inherit the earth.

01:03:45.210 --> 01:03:46.870
Science contradicts that, Doctor.

01:03:48.240 --> 01:03:52.470
Nature proves that the weak must die so that the strong may live.

01:03:53.800 --> 01:03:59.960
Authority, cleverness, imagination, those are the reasons.

