01:12:15.520 --> 01:12:20.300
Becker, Stack, Collins, Coy, Go.

01:12:30.030 --> 01:12:40.230
Only a couple of more hours, once together.

01:12:46.010 --> 01:12:46.490
Who's ready?

01:12:51.530 --> 01:12:53.210
Easy, Robert, you got the whole day ahead of you.

01:12:53.510 --> 01:12:54.410
Sure, this is my racket.

01:12:55.390 --> 01:12:55.630
Thanks.

01:13:00.380 --> 01:13:03.230
Soldier, to the right, that switch.

01:13:03.410 --> 01:13:05.360
The brake will handle that switch.

01:13:06.700 --> 01:13:08.820
This is on the other track, the one that leads to the tower.

01:13:09.460 --> 01:13:09.760
Got that?

01:13:10.000 --> 01:13:10.220
Check.

01:13:10.840 --> 01:13:11.700
What's all that chatter?

01:13:11.940 --> 01:13:13.160
Just wondering what time it was.

01:13:13.340 --> 01:13:14.680
Why? You working by the hour?

01:13:30.860 --> 01:13:31.400
Morning, fellas.

01:13:31.600 --> 01:13:32.040
Hiya, Louie.

01:13:37.070 --> 01:13:37.890
Morning, Chavey.

01:13:38.030 --> 01:13:38.910
Another story?

01:13:39.150 --> 01:13:40.110
Yeah, but this is a good one.

01:13:40.210 --> 01:13:40.790
Hiya, fellas.

01:13:41.050 --> 01:13:41.710
Hello, Louie.

01:13:41.890 --> 01:13:43.670
Finally gonna make your grease monkeys famous.

01:13:43.810 --> 01:13:45.270
Gonna put you all on the front page.

01:13:45.860 --> 01:13:47.000
That's what got us here.

01:13:50.230 --> 01:13:54.330
Tell me, Charlie, what has prison life taught you about being a mechanic?

01:13:55.210 --> 01:13:57.590
It's taught me that when I get out, I shouldn't be a mechanic.

01:14:03.480 --> 01:14:06.080
What about it, Andy? Got anything to say to the press?

01:14:06.520 --> 01:14:08.580
Very much to say. I do as I'm told.

01:14:09.570 --> 01:14:16.720
Everything? Ready to keep your tools.

01:14:33.520 --> 01:14:35.660
Eight firebombs filled with juice. The best.

01:14:36.350 --> 01:14:38.890
Eight fuses. Light, too, as you drive into the yard.

01:14:39.540 --> 01:14:41.680
I say, I always do as I'm told.

01:14:42.350 --> 01:14:45.240
You go to press at 1215 sharp. I'll be there.

01:14:50.200 --> 01:14:52.520
Tell his name right, Louie. His wife keeps a scrapbook.

01:15:15.630 --> 01:15:17.320
News, some good, some bad.

01:15:20.960 --> 01:15:22.760
Firebombs in the toolbox, truck ready to go.

01:15:22.940 --> 01:15:23.160
Bad.

01:15:23.420 --> 01:15:24.060
No dynamite.

01:15:24.160 --> 01:15:24.500
Gotta have it.

01:15:24.540 --> 01:15:26.000
Not a chance, just gave him the die plan.

01:15:26.080 --> 01:15:26.480
Gotta have it.

01:15:26.480 --> 01:15:27.160
Not enough time.

01:15:32.590 --> 01:15:35.510
Look, Louie, I've got an important assignment for you.

01:15:37.180 --> 01:15:38.740
Get down at the green pipe and see Collins.

01:15:38.960 --> 01:15:39.920
Collins? He's with us.

01:15:40.600 --> 01:15:41.500
Tell him there's no dynamite.

01:15:41.620 --> 01:15:44.990
We go anyway? We'll have to go without it.

01:15:45.930 --> 01:15:48.180
Louie, we've got 45 minutes.

01:15:49.960 --> 01:15:51.760
Think I'd be late for my own coming out party?

01:15:52.040 --> 01:15:58.760
I've already... I've tried to explain, madam.

01:15:59.570 --> 01:15:59.670
No.

01:16:00.000 --> 01:16:03.300
No, I'm sorry. All visiting days have been canceled, even for families.

01:16:03.560 --> 01:16:04.180
Take off your hat.

01:16:04.460 --> 01:16:05.740
I'm here to get it passed, Miss Lawrence.

01:16:05.940 --> 01:16:06.700
Where to this time?

01:16:06.820 --> 01:16:08.840
To the drainpipe. We're doing a special layout.

01:16:09.100 --> 01:16:14.640
Wait a minute, what's wrong?

01:16:15.150 --> 01:16:17.490
Nothing. You want to do a story? We want to help.

01:16:26.130 --> 01:16:29.960
From Munzey's office, whose car? Mr. McCall...

01:16:30.770 --> 01:16:33.540
Okay, pass it through. What's the matter with him?

01:16:34.000 --> 01:16:34.940
Muncie left orders.

01:16:36.180 --> 01:16:38.870
Oh, you wanted to go to the drainpipe, huh?

01:16:39.360 --> 01:16:40.380
Yeah, anything wrong with that?

01:16:40.660 --> 01:16:43.080
Muncie in? In and waiting.

01:16:43.480 --> 01:16:49.190
Come on, wait here.

01:16:54.670 --> 01:16:57.760
Drainpipe. 7033, Convict Miller.

01:17:01.240 --> 01:17:01.940
Gallagher's man?

01:17:02.820 --> 01:17:04.600
He was looking for a pass in the warden's office.

01:17:07.280 --> 01:17:10.140
You want to see him now?

01:17:11.320 --> 01:17:12.990
Yeah, bring him in.

01:17:31.400 --> 01:17:33.460
I understand you're interested in the drain pipe.

01:17:33.790 --> 01:17:36.860
Yes, sir. I don't get this, Captain.

01:17:38.380 --> 01:17:41.560
We're planning a big spread on the different kinds of work the cons are doing.

01:17:42.710 --> 01:17:46.440
Oh, that's right. You are a reporter, aren't you, Murray?

01:17:47.240 --> 01:17:47.540
Yes, sir.

01:17:49.180 --> 01:17:49.580
Sit down.

01:17:53.100 --> 01:17:54.270
I'm not there. Here.

01:17:56.560 --> 01:17:57.400
What's the point, Captain?

01:17:58.090 --> 01:17:59.970
I've been to the drain pipe before. I've been to...

01:18:00.000 --> 01:18:06.480
there a hundred times. What's the idea of all this? Tell me, Louie, how does an illiterate like you

01:18:06.480 --> 01:18:18.610
become a reporter? Even a star reporter? I don't know, sir. I do. What business did you have in

01:18:18.610 --> 01:18:28.130
the drainpipe? I told you. Tell me again. To write a story. That answer.

01:18:46.730 --> 01:18:47.070
Thanks, Jason.

01:19:01.180 --> 01:19:03.600
Gallagher sent you to the drain pipe to see somebody.

01:19:05.100 --> 01:19:05.560
Who was it?

01:19:06.090 --> 01:19:06.410
Nobody.

01:19:06.850 --> 01:19:08.150
Just the right answer.

01:19:12.200 --> 01:19:13.060
Leave me alone, Captain.

01:19:13.320 --> 01:19:13.520
Please.

01:19:14.250 --> 01:19:15.870
I don't have the answers you want.

01:19:19.590 --> 01:19:19.890
No?

01:19:49.680 --> 01:19:51.420
Who was it Gallagher sent you to see?

01:19:51.640 --> 01:19:53.790
I told you. Nobody.

01:19:54.430 --> 01:19:55.630
He gave you a message. What was it?

01:19:56.500 --> 01:19:59.500
There was no message. I don't know what you're talking about.

01:20:00.570 --> 01:20:02.070
You don't know much about anything, do you?

01:20:02.210 --> 01:20:02.510
No!

01:20:03.760 --> 01:20:08.580
I suppose you don't even know that Collins plans to break out of the drain pipe at 1215 today, do you?

01:20:09.690 --> 01:20:10.030
No.

01:20:12.120 --> 01:20:12.440
Do you?

01:20:35.440 --> 01:20:38.430
been lying to me, haven't you? Gallagher does

01:20:38.430 --> 01:20:39.990
know something about the break, doesn't he?

01:20:42.660 --> 01:20:49.640
I don't know what you're talking about. You can hit me.

01:20:51.800 --> 01:20:56.600
I'm hitting me. I don't know what you want.

01:21:24.480 --> 01:21:29.850
the isolation ward. Spread the word that he had an accident coming back from the drain.

01:21:30.720 --> 01:21:34.780
Any connection between Gallagher and Collins?

01:21:38.060 --> 01:21:42.060
No. If there was, he would have told me.

01:21:45.750 --> 01:21:47.460
Okay, get the man out of here.

01:21:48.050 --> 01:21:49.200
Hey, you! Muggsy!

01:21:49.340 --> 01:21:58.670
Anything for me? Sure. Sure, Joe.

01:22:00.090 --> 01:22:03.940
Anything wrong with you? No.

01:22:06.390 --> 01:22:18.480
Back to work, Doc.

01:22:19.640 --> 01:22:21.500
Martyogram just came back from the lab, Cullen.

01:22:21.870 --> 01:22:23.440
Yeah? I have to check you again.

01:22:23.720 --> 01:22:24.580
Make a snappy, Doc.

01:22:25.450 --> 01:22:27.210
Okay, okay, keep it moving.

01:22:36.810 --> 01:22:38.790
It was big, nothing.

01:23:10.330 --> 01:23:10.770
picked up.

01:24:30.160 --> 01:24:43.800
position do you want? You're the boss. What are you saying? Make your pick for the break. Position.

01:24:44.810 --> 01:24:57.720
I said I'd play along with you, Joe. You name it. Same goes for me. You got a few minutes, freshman.

01:25:00.000 --> 01:25:00.740
What position do you want?

01:25:01.030 --> 01:25:02.650
I want to give all the help by Kenjo.

01:25:03.710 --> 01:25:03.990
What position?

01:25:05.070 --> 01:25:07.540
To be the toughest winner, Kenjo.

01:25:08.760 --> 01:25:09.040
The best.

01:25:39.050 --> 01:25:47.880
he got hurt banged up they say coming back from the drain pipe coming back yeah Muncie keep circulating

01:26:04.360 --> 01:26:28.770
wouldn't have a better chance.

01:26:30.760 --> 01:26:38.630
oh sorry captain i didn't see you there that's all right hopkins but just remember there's no

01:26:38.630 --> 01:26:42.660
reward for bringing him back alive not in this jungle yes

01:27:03.480 --> 01:27:05.980
Bradley, join the guard along that section of the wall.

01:27:06.080 --> 01:27:06.380
Yes, sir.

01:27:30.500 --> 01:27:31.140
Ready to go.

01:27:31.340 --> 01:27:33.760
Ready to go.

